4d80d87942d2bc731ec46cd0e6d92ea3516","finding_commits":{"inline:4308246261":"8103a0fb3ae9077ec469faf7798958b00e83e1f2","review:5564355456":"8103a0fb3ae9077ec469faf7798958b00e83e1f2"},"parent":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","patch_sha256":"7f52f39db3fe26feb0f487ac17b284d80d87942d2bc731ec46cd0e6d92ea3516","tree":"8fe70e21c24db4a97af06b6bf90e82b554dc6fc6"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"The overview points to the same missing cross-thread JMS coverage as inline:4308246261. Commit 1 adds installed-agent javax and jakarta tests for worker-thread success and failure, both after send returns and while the sender instrumentation scope remains open. The lifecycle implementation required no production change: the tests verify captured caller context, worker/sender context restoration, and one send span plus one duration and sent-message observation despite a later conflicting callback.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5564355456"},{"analysis":"Confirmed the existing deferredCompletion tests only changed context on the sending thread. Commit 1 adds four named crossThreadCompletion cases to each installed-agent suite. A separate executor thread is asserted explicitly; bounded latches publish the wrapped listener and deterministically hold the sender scope open for overlapping completion. Callback assertions check the captured caller context, restore an unrelated worker context with a valid span, and leave sender contexts intact. Future.get propagates worker assertion failures. Each case invokes a conflicting late terminal callback and reuses assertSend/assertSendMetrics to require exactly one send span, duration histogram observation, and sent-message count. Both 32-case suites passed, and all eight new cases passed a focused repeat.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4308246261"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"e67fe25ebcc3a454dec02d3f6b73faf958aac90012fcb3ec45d1c1f680500f07","schema":2},"download_sha256":"91c9187717d59433a8e0d75911188eb363b6d5e380a366b2f2b026e4f81cbc04","frozen_sha":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","pr":20678,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"e67fe25ebcc3a454dec02d3f6b73faf958aac90012fcb3ec45d1c1f680500f07","request_id":"64857ab4d47441368698de191ddd2ab6","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39156544701,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:91c9187717d59433a8e0d75911188eb363b6d5e380a366b2f2b026e4f81cbc04","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39158691528},"workflow_revision":"9c5098a3d18066ad5638649233da6db52445d29f"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5560893133,5564355456],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nJMS cross-thread completion remains untested, and the callback lifecycle changes warrant human review.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add cross-thread JMS callback tests for context propagation and telemetry](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20678#discussion_r4308246261) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5564355456","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5564355456},{"body":"[Testing] Both new `JmsAsyncProducerTest` suites invoke completion callbacks on the sending thread. Changing a context value to `\"callback-thread\"` does not test the thread handoff introduced here. Add installed-agent tests for javax and jakarta JMS that invoke success and failure callbacks on a worker thread, with deterministic synchronization. Verify that the callback sees the captured caller context, restores the worker's previous context, leaves the sender's context intact, and records exactly one send span and metric observation. Include a callback overlapping the send to cover completion while the sender's scope is still open.","comment_commit_id":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","comment_id":4308246261,"key":"inline:4308246261","kind":"inline","line":71,"original_commit_id":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","original_line":71,"path":"instrumentation/jms/jms-common-1.1/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/jms/common/v1_1/JmsSendOperation.java","review_commit_id":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","review_id":5564355456,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-18T18:47:41Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"257c05a0b6d4e69d3e3248d37acc47744d5dd1526533af521fa63bd589e28540","id":4308246261,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-18T18:47:41Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86ttWZm"}],"frozen_at":1792349734,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-18T18:55:34Z","frozen_sha":"0232bd74bc75f926c63441986f1947eaebb3ee58","head_ref":"copilot/fix-missing-error-type-paths","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39155165008},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nRecord missing `error.type` on failed Camel and Lambda SQS message operations, and defer JMS asynchronous send completion until the terminal callback. Apply classification to spans and existing matching metrics without marking recovered exchanges or successful partial-batch invocations failed.\n\n- **Camel:** Classify exception-free terminal faults as `_OTHER`, including metrics emitted when route spans are suppressed; retain exception classification.\n- **Lambda SQS:** Preserve false per-message outcomes through completion, setting `ERROR` and `_OTHER` without affecting successful messages or the enclosing invocation.\n- **JMS:** Finish sends exactly once on callback or synchronous throw. Restore the caller\u2019s context around callbacks so subsequent sends remain instrumented; preserve callback exceptions and JMS 1.1 compatibility.","title":"Fix messaging error classification and JMS asynchronous send completion"},"mode":"publish","pr":20678,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792348792,"generation":2,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"cbf1cbac87bc46dd97ec3685d19628dd","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"64857ab4d47441368698de191ddd2ab6","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/9c5098a3d18066ad5638649233da6db52445d29f","workflow_revision":"9c5098a3d18066ad5638649233da6db52445d29f"},"review_request":{"baseline_review_ids":[5560893133,5564355456,5564593793],"baseline_run_ids":[39158795656,39158795735,39158795794,39158795937,39158795944],"claim":"bfb771394b5f4d65b9c3080df9087e77","confirmation":{"kind":"submitted_review","review_ids":[5564608707]},"owner":{"attempt":"1","run_id":"39158691528"},"recorded_a